    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the info. i checked the vents and they seem to be blowing okay, but it still feels like the air isn't reaching the room effectively. could there be something hidden behind the walls or in the attic messing with the airflow? like a blockage or something we cant see?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, unseen issues in the structure or attic can definitely disrupt airflow. Restricted ductwork hidden in the attic, such as collapsed or improperly sealed joints, is a very common culprit. Heat buildup in an uninsulated attic space can also superheat the air before it enters the system, making conditioning difficult. Inspecting the main duct runs and attic insulation is the next logical step for a more thorough diagnosis.",
      "source": "target",
