      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Unexpected internal heat loads are another major variable to consider. High-wattage electronics, like computers or entertainment centers, in that room can generate significant heat. Furthermore, if the HVAC system has an unbalanced return air path, the pressure might be pulling air away from that specific zone. Testing the system's static pressure or consulting with an HVAC professional can uncover these subtle air dynamics problems.",
      "source": "target",
